            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "Thanks awesome solution @echasnovski \n\nThough I'd like to disagree. `T` is more tedious to write than `t` so `T` should be seen as something less common right?\nIn my +20 years of web development, replacing a tag name vs replacing tag name + all attributes is roughly a 99 against a 1.\n\nIMHO the default `gstt` should only replace the tag name and preserve all attributes because again, that's the most common thing and what people would expect.\n\nNow people would use `sdT` to delete the whole thing but again `T` is less common, so is the deletion feature. I want to bet that most user use mini-surround in html to rename, there are so many more ways to delete a tag like just line deletion, visual selection + `c` or using tree sitter, etc... \n\n`t` and `T` should be both implemented with `t` defaulting to only tag name.\nit's a bummer that not only we need to implement `T` ourselves but also so it works as expected...",
