            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid, the current behavior with not change. Every built-in surrounding has to be consistent across all actions:\n- \"Add\" should the whole tag structure (i.e. `<tag_name>` + `</tag_name>`) on left and right. Not only a single tag name.\n- \"Delete\" should be able to delete the whole tag structure. Deleting only tag name will make the result not valid.\n- \"Replace\" shares the same logic as \"delete\" when it comes to determining which regions should be replaced. So it is fixed on the full tag structure.\n\nThe suggested solution of separate surrounding for a tag name is a reasonable compromise here, I believe.",
